[6672]="700268BF\n1\tDestroy the source of the wailing noises\tLocate and destroy the source of the wailing noises.\n",
[6673]="7002685D\n1\tInvestigate the source of the wailing noises\tPatrons have already begun complaining of the noises in the cellar. Explore the area and see if you can uncover the source of the noises.\n2\tExplore the depths below The Forsaken Inn\tThe book-shelf was hiding a secret passage leading down into the earth below the Inn. You should explore this cavern and see if you can locate who or what is making those noises.\n3\tTalk to the suspicious man\tYou have found a suspicious-looking man reading a book and staring at the glowing, rune-marked door in front of him. Who is this man, and why is he down here? You had best ask him.\n4\tContinue to explore the caverns\tUmín, the man you met in these caverns, has agreed to assist you in your exploration of this place. You must use his expertise to make your way deeper into the caverns.\n5\tBring Umín to the burial chamber\tYou have discovered what appears to be a burial chamber. Perhaps Umín could shed some light on this place.\n6\tPress onwards through the caverns\tUmín has been crushed by the cave-in. You must press on without him. You are on your own now, so be always on guard.\n7\tDefeat Umín\tIt is Umín. Alive and well, it seems... too well even. It appears that he has gained an almost supernatural strength in his absence. He wears a red, glowing necklace around his neck. He is also a bit angry with you... you will have to defeat him if you want to survive.\n8\tTalk to Umín\tThe spinning blade-trap has knocked the necklace from Umín's neck, and it lies glowing on the floor. Umín himself lies crumpled on the floor. Why did he attack you? Speak with him and allow him to explain....\n",
[6674]="70026862\n1\tInvestigate the source of the wailing noises\tPatrons have already begun complaining of the noises in the cellar. Explore the area and see if you can uncover the source of the noises.\n2\tExplore the depths below The Forsaken Inn\tThe book-shelf was hiding a secret passage leading down into the earth below the Inn. You should explore this cavern and see if you can locate who or what is making those noises.\n3\tTalk to the suspicious man\tYou have found a suspicious-looking man reading a book and staring at the glowing, rune-marked door in front of him. Who is this man, and why is he down here? You had best ask him.\n4\tContinue to explore the caverns\tUmín, the man you met in these caverns, has agreed to assist you in your exploration of this place. You must use his expertise to make your way deeper into the caverns.\n5\tBring Umín to the burial chamber\tYou have discovered what appears to be a burial chamber. Perhaps Umín could shed some light on this place.\n6\tPress onwards through the caverns\tUmín has been crushed by the cave-in. You must press on without him. You are on your own now, so be always on guard.\n7\tDefeat Umín\tIt is Umín. Alive and well, it seems... too well even. It appears that he has gained an almost supernatural strength in his absence. He wears a red, glowing necklace around his neck. He is also a bit angry with you... you will have to defeat him if you want to survive.\n8\tTalk to Umín\030Escape the ship\tThe spinning blade-trap has knocked the necklace from Umín's neck, and it lies glowing on the floor. Umín himself lies crumpled on the floor. Why did he attack you? Speak with him and allow him to explain....\n9\tDefeat the Spirit of the Necklace\tIt wasn't Umín at all that was trying to kill you. It was the spirt inhabiting the necklace. It was controlling him, making him do its bidding. You must destroy the spirit, lest it escapes from the place and wreaks havoc upon Middle-earth.\n10\tTalk to Umín\tIt is over. The spirit has been defeated. Speak with Umín and explain your victory.\n",
[6675]="7002684B\n1\tTalk to Anlaf about the free ale\tYou will need to be full of ale if you are to pass the time.\n",
[6676]="7001B191\n1\tSearch east of the Pool of Tranquility\030Search the paths north of the Pool of Tranquility\030Search the barrows north of the Pool of Tranquility\tSearch the southern Scuttledells for signs of Hal Tiller. Ivorel suggested a few places where he might most likely be found as part of the mission he was assigned, but she believes that he is most likely dead.\n2\tTalk to Ivorel at her camp\tIvorel is at her camp in the Scuttledells. You should return to Ivorel and show her the pack you found.\n",
[6677]="70008295\n1\tDefeat sickle-flies (total: 8)\tSickle-flies can be found throughout the marshes of Meluinen, south of Lin Giliath. You should abate the threat of the sickle-flies of Meluinen, which have been stirred to anger by the Stone-trolls.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated several angered sickle-flies in Meluinen, which should give the Elves of Lin Giliath some small respite from the hostile creatures in the glade.\n",
[6678]="70017533\n1\tDeliver the chitin to Mallas at the Shadowed Refuge\tMallas is at the Shadowed Refuge. You should bring the chitin to Mallas. Perhaps he can provide insight as to why there would be insects near the infected Orcs.\n",
[6679]="700686A6\n1\tTalk to Gûshida across the way from Ezôti\tEzôti has revealed where he keeps his captive animals. Share this information with Gûshida. Gûshida is in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tMeet with Gûshida inside Ezôti's Flat\tGûshida told you to meet her at Ezôti's hiding place. Ezôti's hiding place is inside an unassuming flat in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl, to the north-east.\n3\tCheck on the cave-claw\030Check on the goat\030Check on the boar\030Check on the bear\tEzôti's captive animals are in poor condition. Gûshida has asked you to help check on them. Ezôti's hiding place is inside the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n4\tTalk to Gûshida inside Ezôti's Flat\tYou have inspected the animals and should report back to Gûshida. Gûshida can be found in Ezôti's hiding place in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[6680]="7007251C\n1\tSpeak with Viznak at the Sul Madásh in Adagím\tIrsinith enlists you to gain Viznak's aid in learning more about the missing section of the map. Return to him at Sul Madásh.\n2\tCollect a peculiar-looking mushroom from south-east Adagím\tViznak directs you to scour the area in the south-east section of Adagím in search for something out of the ordinary. He believes that you will find a fungal growth very different from the others near the location not on the maps.\n3\tDeliver the peculiar mushroom to Viznak at Sul Madásh\tYou discovered a mushroom at the foot of the mountains in south-eastern Adagím. The mushroom was certainly different and out of place from the rest. Return the mushroom to Viznak at the Mother's Hill.\n",
[6681]="70072F01\n1\tExamine the banner at the ship-yard of Starkhaven\tStanding by a banner on the north-western side of Starkhaven, you decide to explore the ship-yard and learn what you can of its workings.\n2\tExplore north-west frame construction\030Explore western timber assembly\030Explore western central scaffolding\030Explore the central keep of Starkhaven\030Explore eastern central scaffolding\030Explore the south-east forges\030Explore south-east frame construction\030Explore eastern timber assembly\tThe ship-yard at Starkhaven sprawls along the shore at Sûg Nidar, birth-place of a mighty fleet.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have explored the inner workings of the ship-yard at Starkhaven, and learned much of how such a mighty fleet could be constructed.\n",
[6682]="700686DA\n1\tSmack the bags of rice (0/5)\tA merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags. His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.\n2\tSmack the bags of rice (1/5)\tA merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags. His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.\n3\tSmack the bags of rice (2/5)\tA merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags. His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.\n4\tPick up the bag of bad rice\tYou have found a bag of rice that does not pass muster. Pick it up and drop it next to the injured merchant. The injured merchant can be found outside the Monger's Guild-hall in the Upper Ward.\n5\tSmack the bags of rice (3/5)\tA merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags. His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.\n6\tSmack the bags of rice (4/5)\tA merchant has hurt his back and wants you to inspect them in his stead by smacking the bags. His bags of rice can be found arrayed beyond the Wharf-gate just inside the Sail-haven.\n7\tTalk to the injured merchant outside the Monger's Guild-hall\tYou have inspected all the rice and should report back to the injured merchant. The injured merchant is outside the Monger's Guild-hall in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[6683]="70040DF0\n1\tTry to catch a glimpse of Barían\tRhovendol mentioned that Barían could often be found in the Mason's Quarter in Dol Amroth. You should see if you can catch a glimpse of Barían before you run off to take notes on things that resemble her.\n2\tMeditate at the fountain\tThe great fountain of Dol Amroth is in the Court of the Fount. You should meditate at the fountain, and think of how it reminds you of Barían.\n3\tWrite about how the stream of water is strong and bold\tYour journal is in your inventory. You should use the journal to write down your observations.\n4\tExamine the blue canopy for resemblance to Barían\tBlue canopies can be found in the Court of the Fount. You should examine the canopies for resemblance to Barían.\n5\tWrite about the fabric's strength against the wind\tYour journal is in your inventory. You should use the journal to write down your observations.\n6\tLook at the stonework detail on the fine building\tThe building whose stone detail caught your eye is south-east of the fountain in the Court of the Fount -- the one with the golden statue atop it. You should look at the detail on this fine building.\n7\tWrite about the fair stonework's resemblance to Barían\tYour journal is in your inventory. You should use the journal to write down your observations.\n8\tBring your notes to Rhovendol\tRhovendol is in the Scholar's Quarter in Dol Amroth. You should return to Rhovendol.\n",
[6684]="70028267\n1\tTalk to Nia at Lhan Bach\030Talk to Parru at Lhan Bach\tNia and Parru are elders of Lhan Bach, found along the path south of Lhucu's hut. Lhucu asked you to speak with Nia and Parru and convince them to turn away from the service of Trehéarn Brenin.\n2\tTalk to Lhucu at her hut in the Bonevales\tLhucu is at her hut, north of Lhan Bach. You should return to Lhucu with the answers from Nia and Parru.\n",
[6685]="70005D56\n1\tTalk to Postman Oddfoot\tPostman Oddfoot is in Frogmorton, east of Bywater. Postman Cotton is concerned for his friend Oddfoot and wants you to bring word of your efforts to revitalize the Quick Post service in hopes that it will cheer him up.\n",
[6686]="700539ED\n1\tTalk to Vëamacil\tVëamacil and his brothers are at Díngarth.\n2\tTalk to Meldaran\tMeldaran is at Díngarth.\n3\tListen to the conversation of the sons of Isildur\tThe sons of Isildur are at Díngarth.\n4\tTalk to Tárandil\tTárandil is at Díngarth.\n5\tListen to the conversation of the sons of Isildur\tThe sons of Isildur are at Díngarth.\n6\tTalk to Vëamacil\tVëamacil is at Díngarth.\n7\tSit by the fire\tThe sons of Isildur are at Díngarth, waiting for you to sit by their camp-fire.\n8\tListen to the conversation of the sons of Isildur\tThe sons of Isildur are at Díngarth.\n",
[6687]="70052D8B\n1\tTalk to Gírta\tTalk to Gírta.\n2\tHelp set the table.\t\n3\tEnjoy a moment's rest\tEnjoy a moment's rest.\n4\tSit down for a meal\tSit down for a meal.\n5\tTalk to Grimbeorn\tTalk to Grimbeorn.\n6\tEnjoy a meal\tEnjoy a meal.\n",
[6688]="7006EB8D\n1\tSpeak with Mizâdi to continue your ascent through the tower\tGo with Mizâdi up the tower stairs to confront Okhíso.\n2\tAlert Mizâdi you are prepared to continue\tGo with Mizâdi up the tower stairs to confront Okhíso.\n3\tTell Mizâdi you are prepared to move forward\tGo with Mizâdi up the tower stairs to confront Okhíso.\n4\tAssist Mizâdi with her confrontation with Okhíso\tFinish your ascent and enter the tower room to confront Okhiso.\n5\tListen to Mizâdi and Okhíso\tListen to Mizâdi and Okhíso.\n6\tDefeat Okhíso's guards and archers.\t\n7\tListen to Okhíso's dying words\tListen to Okhíso's dying words.\n8\tSpeak with Mizâdi in the tower\tSpeak with Mizâdi in the tower.\n",
